# M2 Pharmacological Dynamics Intelligence Report

## 1. Executive Summary & Epistemic Boundaries

This dossier summarizes an 80-replica, 1,600-stream receptor-side analysis of the GLP-1R Aleniglipron program, including the 5.62-billion spike extraction and downstream tensor fusion.

Following the unprecedented 16.3% weight loss achieved in the ACCESS II trials, Aleniglipron's transition to Phase 3 introduces population-scale pharmacogenomic (PGx) risk. This dossier provides the computational infrastructure to de-risk this Phase 3 expansion by separating potency, durability, and variant-conditioned receptor-state resilience.

Strict Boundary: This dossier provides computationally bounded receptor-side mechanistic evidence. It does not claim in vivo clinical durability. All findings are subject to the explicit wet-lab falsification gates defined in Section 8.

