Aleniglipron represents a classic **Potency Trap**. While it achieves best-in-class potency (`<0.1 nM` in the bounded hGLP-1R cAMP input used here), the 80-replica field assigns a PRISM Durability Risk Score of `{{ "%.0f"|format(clinical_correlation.comparison_table[0].prism_durability_risk_score) }}`. This score indicates that tight activation potency is not equivalent to receptor-state durability; the molecule is projected to carry desensitization risk that EC50 alone cannot resolve.

